      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Keweenaw National Historical Park Visitor Center, housed in an old Oddfellows lodge, chronicles the region’s mining heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calumet%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Three railroads—Copper Range, Hecla & Torch Lake, and Mineral Range—shipped ore from Calumet’s mines to stamp mills, powering the copper boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calumet%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Calumet’s historic district, a National Historic Landmark, preserves most of the village’s original streets and buildings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
